;;; Written for this review (generated, N = 3): a join on a name: (p ?x) (q ?x ?y), each ?x an atom. The index keys (q, slot 0) = a<i>, so the second premise is a bucket lookup.

(p a0)
(p a1)
(p a2)
(q a0 b0)
(q a1 b1)
(q a2 b2)

(rule j () :match (and (p ?x) (q ?x ?y)) :assert (hit ?y) :why "{?y} is paired with what p holds of")

